WEBVTT

00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:06.674
The Grand Exile was constructed

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:11.554
by the consensus of the Ades Federation,
the rightful owner of this world,

00:00:11.804 --> 00:00:14.640
to surpass all else.

00:00:14.891 --> 00:00:17.560
In the name of Maestro Siré,

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.480
a legitimate heir and plenipotentiary
over all inhabitants of this world,

00:00:21.731 --> 00:00:25.902
I hereby declare:

00:00:26.152 --> 00:00:29.238
As of this moment, all acts of
hostility throughout the world

00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:33.034
are to be halted immediately.

00:00:33.284 --> 00:00:38.080
All forces worldwide will
disarm at once and surrender.

00:00:38.331 --> 00:00:43.461
Those who refuse to comply will
face punishment by the Grand Exile.

00:00:43.711 --> 00:00:47.048
All offensive weaponry will be destroyed,

00:00:47.298 --> 00:00:51.302
ushering in an era of true world peace.

00:00:51.552 --> 00:00:55.056
True peace, my ass! You bird-brained bastard!

00:00:55.306 --> 00:00:58.559
He's saying one thing but doing another!

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:03.648
This isn't the peace Sire“! wanted!

00:01:06.359 --> 00:01:09.695
She's crying...

00:01:13.241 --> 00:01:19.830
<i>Soko ni nani ga aru toshite mo</i>

00:01:20.081 --> 00:01:28.506
<i>Mikai no ryouiki e kimi to</i>

00:01:36.764 --> 00:01:44.814
<i>Mijikai yume wo miteta ima</i>

00:01:45.064 --> 00:01:49.443
<i>Are wa kimi no senaka</i>

00:01:49.694 --> 00:01:55.616
<i>Kako? Mirai?</i>

00:01:55.866 --> 00:02:06.377
<i>Furikitte iru meetaa no hari wo mushi shite</i>

00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:09.505
<i>Oikaze to kanjou no muku hou e</i>

00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:15.678
<i>Habataku tabi kizukasareru</i>

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:21.225
<i>Nido to deaenai sora ga aru koto</i>

00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:26.731
<i>Sore demo tobitatsu nara</i>

00:02:26.981 --> 00:02:33.529
<i>Kimi no tsubasa ni naru watashi ga</i>

00:02:52.298 --> 00:02:53.674
Grand Exile's position confirmed!

00:02:53.924 --> 00:02:55.634
Northeastern Glacies, Grid G-7!

00:02:55.885 --> 00:02:59.972
Moving south-southeast by east at 20 knots!

00:03:00.222 --> 00:03:05.311
Admiral Sadri's 1st Fleet has
taken formation ahead of it!

00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:09.732
We cannot let that slaughterer
represent the Augusta any further!

00:03:15.446 --> 00:03:19.992
All ships will focus on eliminating the
enemy fleet at the fore of the Grand Exile!

00:03:20.242 --> 00:03:22.703
Meanwhile, we Vanship pilots
will penetrate its defenses

00:03:22.953 --> 00:03:25.289
and attempt to locate and rescue Augusta Sire-l!

00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:28.501
Gotta scratch that itch to
get back into action, huh?

00:03:28.751 --> 00:03:33.798
We're the only ones with proper
Vanship training who can storm the ship.

00:03:34.048 --> 00:03:36.342
I wish I could play, too...

00:03:36.592 --> 00:03:38.344
The Silvius is in your hands.

00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:41.013
Lend Commander-in-Chief Millia
your support, okay?

00:03:41.263 --> 00:03:42.390
R°gefl

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.474
Oww...

00:03:43.724 --> 00:03:47.895
Cecily. Your ears will be vital inside the blizzard.

00:03:48.145 --> 00:03:51.190
--We're counting on you.
--Yes, Sir! I'll do my utmost!

00:03:51.273 --> 00:03:56.654
Augusta Sire“! is the key to the Grand Exile.

00:03:56.904 --> 00:04:02.493
Alvis Hamilton, another Exile key,
can sense her location.

00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:04.120
Can't you, too?

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.373
You're the new Turan witch, after all.

00:04:07.623 --> 00:04:10.626
I need to command our forces.

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:15.714
Dyan. I would like you to take AI there...

00:04:15.965 --> 00:04:18.384
We have to rescue Sire-l.

00:04:19.969 --> 00:04:22.596
You're our finest pilot.

00:04:22.847 --> 00:04:28.269
You're the only one I can trust with this mission.

00:04:28.519 --> 00:04:30.187
But l...

00:04:33.691 --> 00:04:37.027
Can you really forgive me?

00:04:39.989 --> 00:04:42.241
Dyan...

00:04:42.491 --> 00:04:48.497
No. I can't forgive what you did to my sister yet.

00:04:48.747 --> 00:04:50.082
I can't.

00:04:50.166 --> 00:04:51.876
I can't.

00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:57.131
But I have a duty to fulfill.

00:04:57.381 --> 00:04:59.300
Duty...?

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.344
I absolutely can't run away.

00:05:02.595 --> 00:05:08.225
Because I'm Turan's ruler.
It's my duty to lead its survivors.

00:05:08.476 --> 00:05:13.147
That's what I've inherited from my sister.

00:05:13.397 --> 00:05:16.066
It doesn't matter how I feel!

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.652
It doesn't matter how I feel.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.116
I'm so pitiful.

00:05:27.703 --> 00:05:30.080
<i>I'll fly.</i>

00:05:37.755 --> 00:05:39.840
Everyone's waiting.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:45.638
To everyone about to confront the Grand Exile...

00:05:45.888 --> 00:05:49.892
I believe this <i>will</i> be our final battle.

00:05:50.142 --> 00:05:56.982
Surrendering now might indeed
end the war, as Luscinia claims.

00:05:57.233 --> 00:06:01.278
But could we really call that peace?

00:06:01.529 --> 00:06:06.909
People from different nations--
different worlds-- have gathered here.

00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:13.374
Yet, right now, we all share
the same wish for the same future.

00:06:13.624 --> 00:06:16.794
Surely we know by now that
we can change the world!

00:06:17.044 --> 00:06:21.257
Not by force, but with mutual dialogue...

00:06:21.507 --> 00:06:25.052
...with compassion for each other.

00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:30.558
Together, let us claim our
new future, and then return...

00:06:30.808 --> 00:06:33.769
...to those waiting for us!

00:06:35.771 --> 00:06:38.107
Gisey. I...

00:06:38.357 --> 00:06:41.902
I really want to hold a Grand Race after all.

00:06:42.152 --> 00:06:46.198
Because I think all those
smiles that day were real.

00:06:46.448 --> 00:06:47.908
Fam...

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:50.619
Gisey...!

00:06:50.869 --> 00:06:53.622
Smile, Fam!

00:06:53.872 --> 00:06:55.541
Okay!

00:07:07.761 --> 00:07:09.054
Do you know the controls?

00:07:09.138 --> 00:07:10.973
Fam taught me.

00:07:13.767 --> 00:07:15.477
Now crossing Glacies border!

00:07:15.728 --> 00:07:19.398
ETA to Grand Exile, ten minutes!

00:07:19.648 --> 00:07:21.692
Any word from the Silvius?!

00:07:21.942 --> 00:07:23.652
Unable to confirm!

00:07:23.902 --> 00:07:25.738
Continue to hold formation!

00:07:25.988 --> 00:07:28.907
Keep the comms relay safety margin at 15%!

00:07:29.158 --> 00:07:32.202
Ships detected at 3 o'clock!

00:07:32.453 --> 00:07:34.413
High-speed, heavy flotilla leaders!

00:07:34.663 --> 00:07:39.084
Signal from the
4th Fleet's flagship, the Senapati!

00:07:39.335 --> 00:07:42.838
"Our fleet hereby joins the Joint Forces

00:07:43.088 --> 00:07:47.259
to help create the world of peace
the Augusta and the people desire."

00:07:47.509 --> 00:07:50.971
How mean of you to ditch me, 0l' friend.

00:07:51.221 --> 00:07:53.140
S-Sir!

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.100
Well, I'll be!

00:07:55.351 --> 00:07:56.310
Ships ahead!

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.522
I count 50-- no, 70-- Super-dreadnaughts!

00:08:00.773 --> 00:08:02.441
The 3rd and 4th Fleets!

00:08:05.235 --> 00:08:07.988
There's no freedom in this country!

00:08:08.238 --> 00:08:14.286
Constantly tied down by old edicts,
we do nothing but fight and steal!

00:08:14.536 --> 00:08:16.455
A child like you wouldn't understand!

00:08:16.705 --> 00:08:18.749
This isn't right at all!

00:08:18.999 --> 00:08:21.377
I'm going to soar through skies of my own!

00:08:21.627 --> 00:08:23.879
I won't let anyone get in my way!

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:27.424
Stop, Rahé!

00:08:32.429 --> 00:08:35.766
Perhaps you should have gone
with SorGsh instead, Guzel.

00:08:36.016 --> 00:08:41.605
No. Only the premier can bring
about the world we believe in.

00:08:44.733 --> 00:08:46.902
All hands to battle stations!

00:08:49.405 --> 00:08:52.658
Giant Claudia Unit acoustics ten miles ahead!

00:08:52.908 --> 00:08:55.828
Artillery loading acoustics!
Main gun preparing to fire!

00:08:56.078 --> 00:08:58.330
The Grand Exile...

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.207
All forces, prepare for combat!

00:09:00.457 --> 00:09:01.834
R°gefl

00:09:02.084 --> 00:09:03.919
Now approaching altitude ceiling!

00:09:04.169 --> 00:09:07.631
--Prepare for battle!
--Prepare for battle!

00:09:07.881 --> 00:09:11.468
Assemble the floating docks!
Let's give 'em a foothold!

00:09:15.889 --> 00:09:18.100
Altitude limitation gone!

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.185
Commence Boreas Strategy!

00:09:25.149 --> 00:09:26.608
Fire!

00:09:33.157 --> 00:09:35.534
The enemy is now nearly blind and deaf!

00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:39.455
Give that waygoing old soldier a final farewell!

00:09:44.126 --> 00:09:49.339
Why...? More deaths is
the last thing she wants...

00:09:52.426 --> 00:09:53.761
Incoming enemy fire!

00:09:54.011 --> 00:09:56.764
Impact in three, two, one...!

00:09:59.308 --> 00:10:02.519
High-speed object
approaching at over 300 knots!

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:04.229
Serious threat!

00:10:09.276 --> 00:10:10.486
What?!

00:10:10.736 --> 00:10:13.655
The 4th Fleet's Kuméra
and Guha have been downed!

00:10:13.906 --> 00:10:15.032
What's happening?!

00:10:15.282 --> 00:10:16.867
The Grand Exile is attacking!

00:10:17.117 --> 00:10:21.330
Direct strikes from ultra-high-speed objects!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:24.041
The Grand Exile has them too...

00:10:24.291 --> 00:10:27.169
The Exile defense mechanisms.

00:10:27.419 --> 00:10:29.254
Give the 4th Fleet support!

00:10:30.631 --> 00:10:33.801
Enemy fleet approaching at 10 o'clock!

00:10:34.051 --> 00:10:36.637
Artillery loading acoustics
within the Grand Exile!

00:10:36.887 --> 00:10:38.430
I estimate ten tons or more!

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.558
Alert all ships and order evasive action!

00:10:41.809 --> 00:10:45.062
All comms relays are down!
We're unable to communicate!

00:10:45.312 --> 00:10:46.897
Oh, no...!

00:10:49.274 --> 00:10:50.651
Fan'!

00:10:50.901 --> 00:10:53.195
Isn't there anything <i>we</i> can do?!

00:10:53.445 --> 00:10:56.907
If we go out there now,
we'll be blown to pieces.

00:11:05.332 --> 00:11:08.627
The Augusta's flame will transform this world.

00:11:08.877 --> 00:11:13.966
Not a single opposing ship must be
allowed to approach the Grand Exile!

00:11:14.216 --> 00:11:17.761
Artillery loading complete!
Main gun is about to fire!

00:11:18.011 --> 00:11:19.513
Run, everyone!

00:11:30.691 --> 00:11:32.401
That sound...

00:11:35.487 --> 00:11:37.281
Casualty report!

00:11:37.531 --> 00:11:39.116
We've lost a third of our forces!

00:11:39.366 --> 00:11:42.536
Unusual wind noise from
the Grand Exile's outer hull!

00:11:42.786 --> 00:11:46.999
I believe the gun and its
surrounding shielding have broken off!

00:11:47.249 --> 00:11:49.293
Its gun has?!

00:11:49.543 --> 00:11:53.964
Looks like those big ones are single-use-only.

00:11:54.214 --> 00:11:56.592
Engines to full! Flank speed!

00:11:57.634 --> 00:11:59.678
Engines to full! Flank speed!

00:11:59.928 --> 00:12:02.973
We're sending our intrusion
team through that opening!

00:12:08.395 --> 00:12:12.733
We will launch all Vanships after
we've breached the enemy vessel!

00:12:12.983 --> 00:12:17.821
Once inside the Grand Exile, we'll execute
our plan to retrieve the Augusta!

00:12:18.071 --> 00:12:22.200
Grand Exile gun at 1 o'clock is preparing to fire!

00:12:22.451 --> 00:12:25.120
Target orientation, 191 degrees!

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:26.914
Projected target?!

00:12:27.164 --> 00:12:30.250
The royal city of Turan, lglasia!

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.753
He's planning to destroy Turan again?!

00:12:33.003 --> 00:12:37.132
That isn't a military facility!
Ades immigrants live there, too!

00:12:37.382 --> 00:12:38.926
He's making an example...!

00:12:40.677 --> 00:12:43.180
"That which is born from
the blue surface of water..."

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.266
Replace the combat modules
on all damaged ships at once!

00:12:46.516 --> 00:12:49.853
Incorporate all remaining ships
from the 3rd and 4th Squadrons

00:12:50.103 --> 00:12:52.022
to increase our breakthrough capacity!

00:12:52.272 --> 00:12:53.607
Change of formation.

00:12:53.857 --> 00:12:56.485
Move all heavily damaged ships to the rear.

00:13:00.113 --> 00:13:02.908
"May our serenity be everlasting..."

00:13:03.158 --> 00:13:04.785
Sister...

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:00.757
They used an Exile as a shield...!

00:14:07.139 --> 00:14:09.725
What the...?! What's happening?!

00:14:12.894 --> 00:14:14.646
Something's definitely odd!

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:33.040
Father... Sister... Please safeguard...

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.792
<i>...my dear friends.</i>

00:14:38.086 --> 00:14:39.671
All ships, charge!

00:14:51.558 --> 00:14:52.934
Inverted Wedge formation!

00:14:53.185 --> 00:14:55.312
Fend off the enemy's charge!

00:15:12.537 --> 00:15:16.249
My friends! I've brought the greatest
reinforcements one could hope for!

00:15:23.799 --> 00:15:25.217
Wina!

00:15:25.467 --> 00:15:27.094
Anatoray reinforcements!

00:15:28.386 --> 00:15:30.347
It's about time, Sophia.

00:15:30.597 --> 00:15:35.018
Empress Sophia of Anatoray-Disith
hereby orders all ships...

00:15:35.268 --> 00:15:36.728
...to support the Joint Forces!

00:15:36.978 --> 00:15:38.438
Fly the banner!

00:15:41.274 --> 00:15:43.652
All ships to flank speed!

00:15:43.902 --> 00:15:45.779
Follow the Silvana's lead!

00:15:52.869 --> 00:15:55.413
Thank you for your support!

00:15:55.664 --> 00:15:59.459
Our main focus now is to
get inside the Grand Exile!

00:16:11.805 --> 00:16:13.390
Evade! Five degrees starboard!

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.934
Incoming! 15 degrees up-trim!

00:16:20.814 --> 00:16:23.233
The Silvius must be allowed through!

00:16:35.871 --> 00:16:37.998
All ships will take off
the instant the hatch opens!

00:16:38.248 --> 00:16:39.833
Do not fall behind! Understood?!

00:16:40.083 --> 00:16:41.293
R°gefl

00:16:41.543 --> 00:16:44.838
Output at 80%. All systems are nominal.

00:16:45.088 --> 00:16:47.090
We're all set.

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:49.217
Guess this is it!

00:16:49.467 --> 00:16:51.761
Better hope you're ready, Birdbrain!

00:16:52.012 --> 00:16:53.096
May the wind carry your wings!

00:16:53.346 --> 00:16:55.098
Good tailwinds!

00:16:57.309 --> 00:17:00.228
Don't worry. We're coming now...

00:17:12.282 --> 00:17:14.784
Show 'em what the Swift is made of!

00:17:15.035 --> 00:17:17.579
Lady Millia! Save Augusta Sire-l!

00:17:20.415 --> 00:17:23.710
Ready bow-mounted long-barrel guns!

00:17:28.089 --> 00:17:29.549
Fire!

00:17:39.893 --> 00:17:41.353
All ships, charge!

00:17:56.284 --> 00:17:58.495
We're coming, Siré!

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:04.334
Fam, Giselle, Dyan...

00:18:04.584 --> 00:18:06.086
<i>We're counting on you!</i>

00:18:09.089 --> 00:18:11.716
So this is the Grand Exile...

00:18:11.967 --> 00:18:14.928
It seems familiar somehow...

00:18:28.525 --> 00:18:29.985
Go on, Fam!

00:18:30.235 --> 00:18:32.070
Captain Tatiana!

00:18:39.619 --> 00:18:42.080
I've missed this feeling.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:44.040
Don't get distracted!

00:18:47.544 --> 00:18:49.212
Prepare to ram!

00:18:49.462 --> 00:18:51.840
All hands, brace for impact!

00:19:00.056 --> 00:19:02.183
Just how big is this ship?!

00:19:02.434 --> 00:19:07.731
We gotta hurry! Captain Tatiana, Millia,
and all the others are in danger!

00:19:07.981 --> 00:19:09.482
Just as I thought!

00:19:10.859 --> 00:19:14.112
Yeah, I agree. This isn't right at all.

00:19:14.362 --> 00:19:18.700
You just wanted to create a world
where everyone can smile, didn't you?

00:19:21.828 --> 00:19:23.496
Where to?

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:24.497
That way!

00:19:24.748 --> 00:19:26.166
Wait!

00:19:26.416 --> 00:19:29.252
--Enter the pipe at <i>9</i> o'clock!
--Huh?

00:19:29.502 --> 00:19:32.005
That one will have the shortest route!

00:19:32.255 --> 00:19:34.674
Wha...? How do you know that, Gisey?!

00:19:34.924 --> 00:19:37.344
The Grand Exile seems to share
the same basic structure

00:19:37.594 --> 00:19:40.513
as the Federation flagship Impetus!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:45.810
Fire multi-mount jet-propelled
armor-piercing shells!

00:19:59.407 --> 00:20:00.742
Right turn in eight seconds!

00:20:00.992 --> 00:20:04.329
Five, four, three, two, one...

00:20:04.579 --> 00:20:06.664
Now!

00:20:06.915 --> 00:20:08.375
Left turn in six seconds!

00:20:08.625 --> 00:20:11.336
Four, three, two, one...

00:20:11.586 --> 00:20:12.545
Now!

00:20:12.796 --> 00:20:15.298
Right in five seconds! Three, two, one...

00:20:15.548 --> 00:20:17.008
Now!

00:20:26.142 --> 00:20:29.312
Let <i>us</i> have some bragging rights too, will ya?!

00:20:29.562 --> 00:20:31.898
Bring it on, you birdbrains!

00:20:32.148 --> 00:20:33.733
Take this!

00:20:37.695 --> 00:20:40.281
Go, Fam!

00:20:40.532 --> 00:20:43.368
Guys! May the wind carry your wings!

00:20:58.883 --> 00:21:01.177
Almost there! Just up ahead!

00:21:13.898 --> 00:21:14.816
Dyan!

00:21:14.899 --> 00:21:17.610
Never mind me! Just go!

00:21:27.912 --> 00:21:29.456
Hold on tight!

00:21:45.305 --> 00:21:47.015
End of the line!

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:05.617
Whoa, is this... unfinished?

00:22:05.867 --> 00:22:08.411
It was abandoned during construction...

00:22:08.661 --> 00:22:10.580
Unbelievable...

00:24:01.941 --> 00:24:04.402
<i>Target all guns on the
Grand Exile's interior walls!</i>

00:24:04.652 --> 00:24:05.862
Draw the tentacles' attention to us!

00:24:06.112 --> 00:24:10.116
<i>To unify the world under
Maestro Sari and lead it to peace.</i>

00:24:10.366 --> 00:24:12.493
<i>What point is there to a life
devoid of freedom and free will?</i>

00:24:12.744 --> 00:24:13.911
<i>A life in which you simply "persist"?!</i>

00:24:14.162 --> 00:24:17.415
<i>Indeed, the premier's method
might have the quickest results.</i>

00:24:17.665 --> 00:24:19.792
<i>Are you sure that dream has come to pass?</i>

00:24:20.043 --> 00:24:22.879
<i>The premier himself issued
this order in advance.</i>

00:24:23.129 --> 00:24:25.923
<i>No more people dying!</i>

00:24:26.174 --> 00:24:30.094
But... <i>I</i> want to dream!
